1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:04,337
Hi!

3
00:00:04,387 --> 00:00:06,415
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,536 --> 00:00:11,767
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,079 --> 00:00:15,524
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,574 --> 00:00:18,084
Aladdin and the Wonderful Lamp!

7
00:00:22,707 --> 00:00:27,032
Once upon a time, in a very
old city full of markets,

8
00:00:27,082 --> 00:00:31,718
towers and golden domes, there
lived a boy named Aladdin.

9
00:00:32,375 --> 00:00:38,533
Aladdin was poor, but he had an enormous
smile, and he spent his days running

10
00:00:38,583 --> 00:00:42,761
through the streets, looking at
everything with great curiosity.

11
00:00:43,450 --> 00:00:48,497
His mother worked all day long spinning
cotton, to buy bread and a little

12
00:00:48,547 --> 00:00:49,747
olive oil.

13
00:00:50,298 --> 00:00:55,095
Popcorn the owl, who loved the markets
of the city, liked to perch on a

14
00:00:55,145 --> 00:00:58,531
striped awning and watch everyone go by.

15
00:00:59,182 --> 00:01:04,827
One morning, a tall man with a long grey
beard and a dark green cloak stopped

16
00:01:04,877 --> 00:01:06,707
right in front of Aladdin.

17
00:01:07,235 --> 00:01:10,081
Are you the son of the tailor
who lived on this street?

18
00:01:10,305 --> 00:01:14,447
I am your uncle, and I have come
from very far away just to meet you,

19
00:01:14,497 --> 00:01:18,813
the man in the green cloak
said, with a strange smile.

20
00:01:19,469 --> 00:01:21,980
But that man was nobody's uncle:

21
00:01:22,046 --> 00:01:27,169
he was a magician, who had come from a
distant land to look for a magic lamp.

22
00:01:27,747 --> 00:01:29,124
Hoo, hoo!

23
00:01:29,209 --> 00:01:33,921
That man in the green cloak doesn't
fool me, he is up to something,

24
00:01:33,971 --> 00:01:36,690
Popcorn said, suspicious.

25
00:01:37,813 --> 00:01:41,319
The next day, the two of
them walked out of the city,

26
00:01:41,369 --> 00:01:45,630
past the gardens, and up into
a valley between the mountains.

27
00:01:48,523 --> 00:01:52,978
There, the magician threw a
strange powder into a fire,

28
00:01:53,092 --> 00:01:57,381
colorful smoke rose up, the
ground shook, and it opened,

29
00:01:57,495 --> 00:02:01,062
showing a smooth stone with
a bronze ring in the middle.

30
00:02:04,227 --> 00:02:07,492
Under this stone there is a
treasure, but only you can go in,

31
00:02:07,542 --> 00:02:10,680
Aladdin, because it was kept
for a boy just like you,

32
00:02:10,730 --> 00:02:12,352
the magician said.

33
00:02:13,002 --> 00:02:17,425
The magician took a silver ring off
his own finger, and put it on Aladdin's

34
00:02:17,475 --> 00:02:18,675
finger.

35
00:02:18,903 --> 00:02:20,770
This ring will protect you.

36
00:02:20,863 --> 00:02:25,081
Down below, you will pass through
a garden, but don't touch anything.

37
00:02:25,359 --> 00:02:29,281
Bring me only an old lamp, which
is burning at the back of the cave,

38
00:02:29,331 --> 00:02:30,953
the magician said.

39
00:02:31,606 --> 00:02:37,626
Aladdin pulled the bronze ring, the stone
lifted, and he went down a staircase

40
00:02:37,676 --> 00:02:39,826
of very old steps.

41
00:02:40,925 --> 00:02:46,797
Down below, Aladdin found the most
beautiful garden anyone has ever seen:

42
00:02:46,854 --> 00:02:50,526
the trees had fruits that
sparkled like colored glass,

43
00:02:50,576 --> 00:02:54,574
and tinkled like crystal
whenever the breeze went by.

44
00:02:58,174 --> 00:03:03,040
Not knowing they were precious stones,
Aladdin filled his pockets with shiny

45
00:03:03,090 --> 00:03:06,574
fruits, thinking of bringing
a present to his mother.

46
00:03:07,234 --> 00:03:12,281
At the back of the cave, in a hole
in the wall, was the old copper lamp,

47
00:03:12,331 --> 00:03:13,564
still burning.

48
00:03:13,956 --> 00:03:18,161
He blew out the flame, and
tucked the lamp inside his tunic.

49
00:03:18,698 --> 00:03:22,789
Give me the lamp first, Aladdin,
and then I'll help you climb out,

50
00:03:22,839 --> 00:03:26,808
the magician shouted from
above, reaching out his hand.

51
00:03:27,448 --> 00:03:31,299
Help me climb out first, uncle, because
my pockets are heavy and the stairs

52
00:03:31,349 --> 00:03:32,304
are very high,

53
00:03:32,354 --> 00:03:33,934
Aladdin answered.

54
00:03:34,594 --> 00:03:39,835
The magician got so angry that he
stamped his foot, said the magic words,

55
00:03:39,885 --> 00:03:43,272
and the stone slammed
shut with a great rumble.

56
00:03:46,561 --> 00:03:52,011
Everything went dark, and without meaning
to, Aladdin rubbed the silver ring,

57
00:03:52,061 --> 00:03:54,836
and a green light filled the cave.

58
00:03:58,420 --> 00:04:02,862
In front of him appeared a small
genie, made of green smoke,

59
00:04:02,948 --> 00:04:06,195
with eyes that glowed like fireflies.

60
00:04:06,828 --> 00:04:10,308
I am the ring genie, and I
obey whoever wears this ring.

61
00:04:10,639 --> 00:04:11,798
What is your wish?

62
00:04:11,848 --> 00:04:13,582
the ring genie said.

63
00:04:14,214 --> 00:04:16,920
I just want to go home,
back to my mother's arms,

64
00:04:16,970 --> 00:04:19,745
Aladdin said, his eyes shining.

65
00:04:20,385 --> 00:04:24,882
In the blink of an eye, Aladdin
was standing at his own front door,

66
00:04:24,968 --> 00:04:29,799
with his pockets full of shiny
fruits and the old lamp in his hand.

67
00:04:30,807 --> 00:04:33,002
We have nothing to eat, son.

68
00:04:33,132 --> 00:04:36,659
Let's sell this old lamp at the
market, but first I'll clean it,

69
00:04:36,709 --> 00:04:38,387
so it's worth a little more,

70
00:04:38,437 --> 00:04:39,865
his mother said.

71
00:04:40,516 --> 00:04:44,707
His mother took a cloth, and
began to rub the lamp hard.

72
00:04:48,308 --> 00:04:53,106
Suddenly, a golden smoke came
out of the lamp, and it grew,

73
00:04:53,156 --> 00:04:56,153
and grew, until it touched the ceiling.

74
00:04:56,319 --> 00:05:01,033
And out of the smoke rose an
enormous genie, the color of amber,

75
00:05:01,083 --> 00:05:05,331
with a beard of smoke and a
deep voice like distant thunder.

76
00:05:05,923 --> 00:05:09,909
I am the lamp genie, and I
obey whoever holds the lamp.

77
00:05:10,145 --> 00:05:12,086
Ask for anything you like,

78
00:05:12,136 --> 00:05:13,897
the lamp genie said.

79
00:05:14,552 --> 00:05:16,665
Dear genie, we are very hungry.

80
00:05:16,882 --> 00:05:18,938
Could you bring us something
delicious for lunch?

81
00:05:18,988 --> 00:05:20,416
Aladdin asked.

82
00:05:21,092 --> 00:05:26,283
At once, the table was covered with
silver plates, with warm bread,

83
00:05:26,383 --> 00:05:30,103
rice with raisins, sweet fruits and honey.

84
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:32,057
Hoo, hoo!

85
00:05:32,168 --> 00:05:36,272
What a wonderful smell, even
my owl tummy is rumbling,

86
00:05:36,322 --> 00:05:39,000
Popcorn said, at the window.

87
00:05:39,666 --> 00:05:42,983
But Aladdin and his mother
did not become greedy:

88
00:05:43,094 --> 00:05:47,508
they lived simply, and only asked the
genie for what they really needed.

89
00:05:48,139 --> 00:05:52,895
In time, Aladdin learned from the jewelers
at the market that the shiny fruits

90
00:05:52,945 --> 00:05:56,345
from the cave were really precious stones.

91
00:05:57,414 --> 00:06:01,800
One day, the princess of the city
passed along the main street,

92
00:06:01,872 --> 00:06:05,328
and stopped to give bread to
some children who were hungry.

93
00:06:05,967 --> 00:06:08,498
Mother, I would love to be
friends with the princess,

94
00:06:08,548 --> 00:06:11,178
because she is the kindest
person I have ever seen,

95
00:06:11,228 --> 00:06:12,698
Aladdin said.

96
00:06:13,358 --> 00:06:17,022
His mother arranged the precious
stones in a porcelain bowl,

97
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:20,341
and carried the present
to the sultan's palace.

98
00:06:20,931 --> 00:06:22,513
How marvelous!

99
00:06:22,652 --> 00:06:26,505
I have never seen such
beautiful stones in all my life,

100
00:06:26,555 --> 00:06:30,649
the sultan said, holding a
red stone up to the light.

101
00:06:31,246 --> 00:06:33,358
My daughter loves stories.

102
00:06:33,510 --> 00:06:38,174
If your son builds a palace full of
books, as beautiful as this present,

103
00:06:38,224 --> 00:06:40,198
the princess will love to visit,

104
00:06:40,248 --> 00:06:42,704
the sultan said, smiling.

105
00:06:43,364 --> 00:06:48,967
That night, Aladdin rubbed the lamp, and
in just a few hours the genie built a

106
00:06:49,017 --> 00:06:55,667
white palace, with windows full of
sparkling stones and an enormous library.

107
00:06:59,265 --> 00:07:04,784
The next day, the whole city had an
enormous party, with music and colorful

108
00:07:04,834 --> 00:07:09,151
lanterns, and Aladdin and the
princess became great friends,

109
00:07:09,306 --> 00:07:12,290
reading stories together every afternoon.

110
00:07:13,381 --> 00:07:17,942
But far away from there, the magician
found out that Aladdin had escaped from

111
00:07:17,992 --> 00:07:22,156
the cave, and that he was
rich, with the magic lamp.

112
00:07:22,832 --> 00:07:28,309
He came back to the city, disguised as
a peddler, with a basket full of shiny

113
00:07:28,359 --> 00:07:29,648
new lamps.

114
00:07:30,181 --> 00:07:31,586
New lamps!

115
00:07:31,712 --> 00:07:34,145
I'll trade new lamps for old ones!

116
00:07:34,195 --> 00:07:38,858
the magician called out, walking
up and down in front of the palace.

117
00:07:39,490 --> 00:07:43,704
That day, Aladdin had gone to
visit the villages near the city,

118
00:07:43,754 --> 00:07:47,432
and the princess was reading
in the palace library.

119
00:07:48,016 --> 00:07:49,679
What a funny peddler!

120
00:07:49,854 --> 00:07:53,479
We have an old lamp here, let's
trade it for a nice new one,

121
00:07:53,529 --> 00:07:55,860
the princess said, laughing.

122
00:07:56,493 --> 00:08:00,791
Hoo, hoo, no, princess,
don't make that trade!

123
00:08:00,841 --> 00:08:07,199
Popcorn cried, flapping her wings, but
nobody understood the language of owls.

124
00:08:07,818 --> 00:08:12,921
The magician rubbed the lamp, and ordered
the genie to carry the whole palace,

125
00:08:12,971 --> 00:08:17,315
with the princess inside, to
the distant land where he lived.

126
00:08:24,144 --> 00:08:28,441
When Aladdin came back, where the
palace had been there was only an empty

127
00:08:28,491 --> 00:08:31,822
field, and the sultan was very worried.

128
00:08:32,914 --> 00:08:37,078
Aladdin rubbed the silver ring,
and the ring genie appeared,

129
00:08:37,150 --> 00:08:38,745
with its green light.

130
00:08:42,324 --> 00:08:45,029
Please, bring back the
palace and the princess,

131
00:08:45,079 --> 00:08:47,340
Aladdin asked the ring genie.

132
00:08:47,983 --> 00:08:51,111
That I cannot do, because
that power is not mine.

133
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:52,896
But I can take you to them,

134
00:08:52,946 --> 00:08:54,679
the ring genie said.

135
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:59,714
In the blink of an eye, Aladdin was
on the other side of the desert,

136
00:08:59,764 --> 00:09:04,053
under the princess's window,
on a night full of stars.

137
00:09:04,650 --> 00:09:06,864
Aladdin, how good to see you!

138
00:09:07,045 --> 00:09:10,034
The magician keeps the lamp
in the pocket of his cloak,

139
00:09:10,084 --> 00:09:12,320
and won't let go of it even to sleep,

140
00:09:12,370 --> 00:09:14,936
the princess said, at the window.

141
00:09:15,619 --> 00:09:17,686
The two of them made a plan:

142
00:09:17,746 --> 00:09:22,376
the princess would serve the magician a
strong, warm cup of chamomile tea with

143
00:09:22,426 --> 00:09:25,715
honey, so that he would fall fast asleep.

144
00:09:26,373 --> 00:09:31,240
That night, the magician drank
the tea, yawned three times,

145
00:09:31,290 --> 00:09:35,732
and fell into a sleep so deep
that he snored like a bear.

146
00:09:36,345 --> 00:09:40,295
The princess took the lamp out of
his cloak pocket very carefully,

147
00:09:40,345 --> 00:09:42,384
and opened the door for Aladdin.

148
00:09:46,140 --> 00:09:49,998
Aladdin rubbed the lamp,
and the lamp genie appeared,

149
00:09:50,057 --> 00:09:52,054
enormous and golden.

150
00:09:55,654 --> 00:09:59,632
Please, carry the palace back to our
city, but leave the magician sleeping

151
00:09:59,682 --> 00:10:00,230
here,

152
00:10:00,280 --> 00:10:02,638
Aladdin asked the lamp genie.

153
00:10:03,311 --> 00:10:09,400
The palace flew over the desert, soft
as a cloud, and landed in its place just

154
00:10:09,450 --> 00:10:11,253
as the sun was rising.

155
00:10:13,801 --> 00:10:18,626
When the sultan saw the palace from
his window, he ran to hug his daughter,

156
00:10:18,676 --> 00:10:21,687
and Aladdin's mother cried with joy.

157
00:10:22,333 --> 00:10:23,817
And the magician?

158
00:10:24,109 --> 00:10:28,037
He woke up in the middle of
the sand, with no palace,

159
00:10:28,087 --> 00:10:30,862
no lamp and no one left to trick.

160
00:10:31,246 --> 00:10:35,571
They say that, ever since, he sells
real lamps, and has learned to work

161
00:10:35,621 --> 00:10:36,821
honestly.

162
00:10:37,378 --> 00:10:41,044
Thank you, genie, but the greatest
treasure I have is my family,

163
00:10:41,094 --> 00:10:42,866
and a clever and kind heart,

164
00:10:42,916 --> 00:10:44,385
Aladdin said.

165
00:10:45,035 --> 00:10:50,610
And Popcorn, perched on a golden
dome, blinked her big eyes and smiled,

166
00:10:50,660 --> 00:10:54,074
because she loved happy endings very much.

167
00:11:01,398 --> 00:11:02,598
The End.

168
00:11:04,313 --> 00:11:05,025
Hoo...

169
00:11:05,075 --> 00:11:06,099
Psst!

170
00:11:06,149 --> 00:11:07,721
Are you still awake?

171
00:11:07,875 --> 00:11:09,929
Did you like tonight's story?

172
00:11:10,061 --> 00:11:14,568
Aladdin showed us that cleverness
and kindness are worth more than any

173
00:11:14,618 --> 00:11:18,898
treasure, and that greed only
ends up losing everything.

174
00:11:19,185 --> 00:11:23,491
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

175
00:11:23,787 --> 00:11:28,685
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

176
00:11:28,735 --> 00:11:31,140
for more stories at bedtime.

177
00:11:31,444 --> 00:11:32,644
Hoo...

